                "stats-run.json: completeCaseN=240, but no mention of initial N"
              ],
              "whyItMatters": "Selective inclusion of complete cases can bias results if missingness is related to exposure or outcome; the absence of any missing-data description prevents assessment.",
              "actionableFix": "Report the number of records excluded due to missing data, describe missingness patterns for each variable, and consider sensitivity analyses (e.g., multiple imputation) or justify the complete-case approach.",
